.TH RUBYC 1 "November 2026" "rubycom 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rubyc \- Ahead-Of-Time Ruby to x86-64 native compiler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rubyc
.I input.rb
[\fB\-o\fR \fIoutput\fR]
[\fB\-\-emit\-asm\fR]
[\fB\-\-run\fR]
[\fB\-\-\fR \fIargs\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rubyc
compiles Ruby source files directly into x86-64 System V ABI assembly and links
them into standalone native ELF64 executables.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-o \fIoutput\fR
Specify the output binary (or assembly file with \fB\-\-emit\-asm\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-emit\-asm, \-S
Emit x86-64 assembly instead of linking an executable.
.TP
.B \-\-run, \-r
Execute the compiled binary immediately after linking.
.SH AUTHOR
Gideon Laurie <gideon.a.e.laurie@gmail.com>
